*> Implementation test of lane bugviewbob (T62400-T62403; docs/protocol/12 section 6.1 steps 1 and 2, 53 section 15.2, 57-1 section 5): VIEW-POSE, the matrix of the hurt and
*> death tilt (outermost) and view bobbing that the world view and the hand start from. The 12 numbers of each scenario (a 3 x 3 rotation by rows, then the translation,
*> in millionths) come from scratchpad/models/view_pose.py (an independent model written from the document text; sway left out: pitch and yaw equal their lagging
*> values); one scenario is the document's own worked example of 53 section 15.2 (translate -0.0155, -0.0951; rotate Z -0.093 and X 0.435 degrees). Option bobView off,
*> a standing player (b = 0) and a player at rest give the identity.
